@startuml

start

:Thermal management controller operates as deterministic state machine within RTOS;
fork
  :Govern PWM fans;
fork again
  :Govern liquid-cooling loops;
end fork

if (Abnormal energy supply(Rail voltage fluctuations > defined threshold for sustained duration with out-of-range ambient temperature)?) then (yes)
  :Initiate multi-threaded response;

  fork
    :High-priority task;
    :Begin real-time power load monitoring;
    :Command PMIC/BMS to execute backup power switching sequence;
  fork again
    :Lower-priority thread synchronized via mutex;
    :Continuously poll backup power status;
    :Energy allocation optimization algorithm dispatched from priority queue;
    :Run deterministically to stabilize supply;
  fork again
    :Enter fault diagnosis mode;
    :Initialize early warning mechanism;
  fork again
    :Timer-driven ISR periodically polls equipment status;
    :Dispatch real-time service reports over CAN bus;
    :Ensure message integrity with CRC;
  end fork

  :Detection and optimization completed;
  :Generate comprehensive energy security service report;
  :Perform holistic evaluation of energy supply network;

else (no)
end if


:Sensor fusion and calibration routines execute periodically;
if (Persistent out-of-range readings?) then (yes)
  :Trigger sensor redundancy protocols;
  :Engage controlled cool-down path managed by FADEC;
else (no)
end if

stop

@enduml
